IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- Row il-74, TARGETED: the Labour Courts Law, 5729-1969 ("the Law"; the English title is a working translation of the Hebrew title the amending instruments print). Draft, target compiler main. No domain expert has read this against the source.
-- THIS ROW DOES NOT ENCODE THE LAW. It records one reference of the Law (item I1: item 1, paragraph (e), of the Third Schedule) as typed values, and tests them.
-- SEAT: the person aggrieved by a decision of the National Insurance Institute on their functional status, the person to whom paragraph (a) of section 230B of the National Insurance Law is written. A row of references asks that person no question: there is no input to ask for, and no @export.
-- NOUNS: an instrument as its footer prints it, a provision of another law, the period of a temporary provision as an instrument prints it, a citation of a section of another law, a day the row computed (never a printed day), an instrument that prints words of the Third Schedule, the item, and the questions asked of them. No reference is stated here; it is in lb74-cross-references.l4.
--
-- The item is recorded with two limbs, as in the other targeted rows:
--   limb (a): the target is repealed, missing or says something else, read from an official instrument;
--   limb (b): the citing words still read so in the latest official instrument read.
-- For this item limb (a) is a comparison of dates: the last period the instruments read print for the cited section ends, by computation, before the day the citing instrument was published. The row compares dates only.
--
-- LATIN LETTERS. The Hebrew of every number and quoted word is on an `ext:` line (read from the deposited page image of an official instrument) or a `src:` line (the deposited excerpt of the consolidation). The modules type the section numbers in Latin letters (tools/translit.py checks the Latin against the Hebrew, line by line):
--   a Hebrew letter alef, bet, gimel or dalet after a digit is A, B, C or D (230B is 230 bet); alef to dalet and he alone in brackets are (a) to (e).
-- Hebrew is typed in code only where the very same words are in the deposited excerpt (tools/hebcheck.py checks that): the citing words and the title of the National Insurance Law.
-- THE NAMES BELOW ARE MINE, not the Law's. A status is what the instruments read give; NotChecked is a value, not an absence: it marks a section the row names and did not read.
-- An instrument is typed as Printed: the row says what a page prints and when its issue is dated, and nothing about any other status.

§ `Nouns`

DECLARE `The status of an instrument as the row types it` IS ONE OF
    Printed

DECLARE `A status in the instruments read` IS ONE OF
    Added
    NotChecked

DECLARE `How a limb was read` IS ONE OF
    `official page images`
    `official page images, with the absence of a later instrument resting on the consolidation's tag list (CONSOLIDATION-ONLY)`

-- The period of 30 months starts on a printed day; the pages do not say whether that day is day 1 of the 30 months or whether they are counted from the next day. The row types both and chooses neither.
DECLARE `A counting convention` IS ONE OF
    `the start day is day 1 of the months`
    `the months are counted from the day after the start day`

-- An instrument as its footer prints it. `the issue date its footer prints` is the date of the issue, never a day of effect.
DECLARE `An instrument` HAS
    `its citation` IS A STRING
    `what it is, in a working translation` IS A STRING
    `the issue date its footer prints` IS A DATE
    `its status as the row types it` IS A `The status of an instrument as the row types it`
    `the printed pages deposited` IS A LIST OF NUMBER

-- A provision of another law that the item cites, or that an item of the Third Schedule names.
DECLARE `A provision` HAS
    `the law it belongs to` IS A STRING
    `its number, with letters in Latin` IS A STRING
    `its status in the instruments read` IS A `A status in the instruments read`
    `the instrument that gives the status` IS A STRING
    `what the status rests on` IS A STRING

-- The period of section 230B as its first instrument prints it: the words give a delay and a length, and no calendar date.
DECLARE `The first period printed for section 230B` HAS
    `the instrument` IS A `An instrument`
    `the section of the instrument that prints it` IS A STRING
    `the delay before the commencement day, in months from publication, as the words print it` IS A NUMBER
    `the length from the commencement day, in years, as the words print it` IS A NUMBER
    `the calendar date the words print for the commencement day` IS A MAYBE DATE

-- The period of section 230B as its second instrument prints it: a start day and a number of months, both printed.
DECLARE `A period printed in months` HAS
    `the instrument` IS A `An instrument`
    `the section of the instrument that prints it` IS A STRING
    `the section of the 2005 law the instrument amends` IS A STRING
    `the day of the month the period starts, as the words print it` IS A NUMBER
    `the month the period starts, as the words print it` IS A NUMBER
    `the year the period starts, as the words print it` IS A NUMBER
    `the number of months, as the words print it` IS A NUMBER

-- A day that no page prints: the row computed it from printed values and says how. It is never typed as a printed day.
DECLARE `A day the row computed` HAS
    `the day` IS A DATE
    `the computation` IS A STRING
    `what it is computed from` IS A STRING

-- The words of an item of a schedule, with the section of another law they name.
DECLARE `A citation of a section of another law` HAS
    `the item` IS A STRING
    `the item of the Third Schedule` IS A STRING
    `the lettered paragraph, with letters in Latin` IS A STRING
    `the instrument that prints the citing words` IS A `An instrument`
    `the printed page of the citing words` IS A NUMBER
    `the citing words` IS A STRING
    `the number of the cited section, with letters in Latin` IS A STRING
    `the cited law, as the opening words of the item print it` IS A STRING

-- An instrument that prints words of the Third Schedule, and the items of the schedule its words name.
DECLARE `An instrument that prints words of the Third Schedule` HAS
    `the instrument` IS A `An instrument`
    `what its words do to the Third Schedule` IS A STRING
    `the items of the Third Schedule its words name` IS A LIST OF STRING

DECLARE `An item of the row` HAS
    `the item` IS A STRING
    `the citation` IS A `A citation of a section of another law`
    `the last period printed for the cited section` IS A `A period printed in months`
    `the instruments read that print words of the Third Schedule` IS A LIST OF `An instrument that prints words of the Third Schedule`
    `limb (a) was read` IS A `How a limb was read`
    `limb (b) was read` IS A `How a limb was read`
    `the instruments and pages read` IS A STRING

-- The questions. Each takes a value from lb74-cross-references.l4.

GIVEN p IS A `A provision`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the provision was not read` MEANS p's `its status in the instruments read` EQUALS NotChecked

GIVEN p IS A `A provision`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the provision is added by an instrument deposited here` MEANS p's `its status in the instruments read` EQUALS Added

GIVEN p IS A `A provision`
GIVETH A STRING
`the number of the provision` MEANS p's `its number, with letters in Latin`

-- The same day of the month, the printed number of months later: 29 September 2009 plus 30 months is 29 March 2012.
-- `Date d m y` rolls a month number past 12 into the next year (daydate.l4 calls that the lenient constructor).
GIVEN p IS A `A period printed in months`
GIVETH A DATE
`the same day of the month, the printed number of months after the start day` MEANS
    Date (p's `the day of the month the period starts, as the words print it`) ((p's `the month the period starts, as the words print it`) PLUS (p's `the number of months, as the words print it`)) (p's `the year the period starts, as the words print it`)

GIVEN p IS A `A period printed in months`
GIVETH A DATE
`the printed start day` MEANS
    Date (p's `the day of the month the period starts, as the words print it`) (p's `the month the period starts, as the words print it`) (p's `the year the period starts, as the words print it`)

-- If the start day is day 1 of the months, the last day is the day before the day the months reach; if they are counted from the day after the start day, it is the day the months reach.
GIVEN p IS A `A period printed in months`
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day of the period if the start day is day 1 of the months` MEANS
    Date ((Day (`the same day of the month, the printed number of months after the start day` p)) MINUS 1)

GIVEN p IS A `A period printed in months`
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day of the period if the months are counted from the day after the start day` MEANS
    `the same day of the month, the printed number of months after the start day` p

GIVEN p IS A `A period printed in months`, c IS A `A counting convention`
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day of the period under the convention` MEANS
    IF c EQUALS `the start day is day 1 of the months`
    THEN `the last day of the period if the start day is day 1 of the months` p
    ELSE `the last day of the period if the months are counted from the day after the start day` p

GIVEN p IS A `A period printed in months`, c IS A `A counting convention`, d IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the last day of the period under the convention is on or after the day` MEANS
    (`the last day of the period under the convention` p c) AT LEAST d

GIVEN p IS A `A period printed in months`, c IS A `A counting convention`, d IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the number of days from the last day of the period under the convention to the day` MEANS
    (Day d) MINUS (Day (`the last day of the period under the convention` p c))

-- Limb (a): under each of the two conventions the last day of the last period printed for the cited section is before the day the citing instrument's footer prints.
GIVEN i IS A `An item of the row`, c IS A `A counting convention`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the last period printed ends before the citing instrument was published under the convention` MEANS
    NOT (`the last day of the period under the convention is on or after the day` (i's `the last period printed for the cited section`) c (i's `the citation`'s `the instrument that prints the citing words`'s `the issue date its footer prints`))

GIVEN i IS A `An item of the row`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`limb (a) holds` MEANS
    (`the last period printed ends before the citing instrument was published under the convention` i `the start day is day 1 of the months`) AND (`the last period printed ends before the citing instrument was published under the convention` i `the months are counted from the day after the start day`)

-- Limb (b): no instrument read that prints words of the Third Schedule, later than the citing instrument, names the item.
GIVEN i IS A `An item of the row`, w IS A `An instrument that prints words of the Third Schedule`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the instrument is later than the citing instrument and names the item` MEANS
    ((w's `the instrument`'s `the issue date its footer prints`) GREATER THAN (i's `the citation`'s `the instrument that prints the citing words`'s `the issue date its footer prints`)) AND (elem (i's `the citation`'s `the item of the Third Schedule`) (w's `the items of the Third Schedule its words name`))

-- The list is walked one instrument at a time (a function with two inputs cannot be handed to `any` half-applied on main).
GIVEN i IS A `An item of the row`, ws IS A LIST OF `An instrument that prints words of the Third Schedule`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`no instrument in the list is later than the citing instrument and names the item` MEANS
    CONSIDER ws
        WHEN EMPTY THEN TRUE
        WHEN w FOLLOWED BY rest THEN (NOT (`the instrument is later than the citing instrument and names the item` i w)) AND (`no instrument in the list is later than the citing instrument and names the item` i rest)

GIVEN i IS A `An item of the row`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`limb (b) holds` MEANS
    `no instrument in the list is later than the citing instrument and names the item` i (i's `the instruments read that print words of the Third Schedule`)

GIVEN i IS A `An item of the row`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`both limbs hold` MEANS `limb (a) holds` i AND `limb (b) holds` i
